  "minimum_window_rationale": "drand Quicknet period = 3 s/round. The protocol-level minimum (enforced in timelock_common.py: minimum_preparation_lead_seconds=1800s and minimum_stage_separation_seconds=1800s) is the absolute floor. The v2 window is adaptation=NOW+30min, final_evaluation=NOW+1h30min, giving a 1-hour separation between stages — 2x the protocol minimum. Justification for choosing 1h separation over the 7-day conservative default: (a) Quicknet 1800-round depth at the protocol floor + 1800-round separation still defeats opportunistic early reveal under BLS threshold signature assumptions; (b) the full v2 mechanism (E1a+E1b+E2 prediction freeze + 2 distinct-device replicas + plaintext chmod-000+rename-sealed-off + GitHub workflow attestation + pre-removal inventory) is in place; (c) the researcher accepts the trade-off of shorter window for the thesis timeline. Disclosure text is committed in v2 freeze-manifest.md §6.",
